{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>The sanctuary of YHWH, Your hands established.</b> Because the Tabernacle was made entirely by the word of YHWH from Him — for in every matter of the Tabernacle it is stated, ״וְהֵקֵמֹתָ אֶת־הַמִּשְׁכָּן כְּמִשְׁפָּטוֹ אֲשֶׁר הָרְאֵיתָ בָּהָר״ (Exodus 26:30) — therefore it says, ״Your hands established.״ And it uses ״Your hands״ — two in meaning — Rashi explained that the world was created with one hand and the Sanctuary with two hands, etc. And in the first chapter of Ketubot (5a) they said: ״Greater are the deeds of the righteous than the act of heaven and earth, for while heaven and earth were created with one hand, as it says (Isaiah 48:13) 'My hand also has laid the foundation of the earth, and My right hand has spanned the heavens,' yet in the deeds of the righteous it is written, 'The sanctuary of YHWH, Your hands established.'״ And the reason for this: the supernal beings, by virtue of their excellence, were created with the right hand, and the lower beings with the left hand. But the Sanctuary, which is the intermediary that joins the supernal and the lower, was created with both hands — for there is the dwelling of the Shekhinah among the lower ones, as it says, ״וְשָׁכַנְתִּי בְּתוֹכָם״ (Exodus 25:8). And from there man too was created, the intermediary between the supernal and the lower beings, and this is the matter of the ladder, ״מֻצָּב אַרְצָה וְרֹאשׁוֹ מַגִּיעַ הַשָּׁמָיְמָה״ (Genesis 28:12), and its middle slope corresponded to the Temple, for it is the intermediary, as stated. And what they called the Sanctuary ״the deed of the righteous,״ while Scripture says ״Your hands established״ — that is, the hands of the Holy One, blessed be He — is because both of them have a share in this building: for the Holy One, blessed be He, showed Moses the pattern of the entire Tabernacle built, as it is written, ״כֵּן עָשָׂה הַמְּנוֹרָה״ (Numbers 8:4) — the Holy One, blessed be He, made it — and so too every part of the work of the Tabernacle."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:20:40.554762565Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}